  "review_notes": [
    "Independently reviewed the current top-level proposal.json, not merely the prior packet embedded in context. Read proposal lines 1-149, functionality lines 1-36, fact-disposition ledger lines 1-385, and link-disposition ledger lines 1-260.",
    "All six proposed writes are supported. The added entry data-flow correction accurately places the second ftCommon_8007E2F4 call after ftColl_8007B760. The other changes correct non-saturating floating countdown behavior, the timeout predicate's false-return contract, timeout destination distinctions, and false-return mutation in the fourth IASA handler.",
    "Read both owned files completely in canonical and rendered forms and enumerated all 14 subjects, 39 baseline facts, and 12 outgoing links. Rendered aliases were not used as independent evidence.",
    "Validated foreign definitions for CliffCatch handoff and delegation, the four input handlers and their entry destinations, the floating cliff fields, RETURN_IF, motion-state callback bindings, Fighter_ChangeMotionState's declaration, ftCommon_8007E2F4, ftColl_8007B760, ftCo_80090780, and ftGetParasolStatus.",
    "The active motion table corroborates DamageFall and the ledge-option callback families. Quick/Slow labels do not establish quantitative animation or gameplay differences. The timeout's non-parasol path is distinct from the explicit ftCo_Fall_Enter calls used by manual drop and invalid-ledge physics.",
    "Boundary analysis is appropriately conditional on ordinary IEEE floating semantics, rather than claiming exceptional values occur in normal gameplay. Equality selects x490; a positive fractional countdown can become negative; NaN fails both countdown and timeout comparisons; positive infinity and sufficiently large finite values need not progress.",
    "The current functionality document repairs the prior malformed ftcoll citation and explicitly defers compiled section layout, optional-path semantics, cooldown consumers, unknown flags, object lifetime, and engine scheduling. Acceptance does not resolve those deferred claims.",
    "Independent dispositions below agree with the current top-level ledgers. Retained broad lifecycle descriptions are read as descriptions of the guarded operations, not as guarantees of finite expiration, false-return purity, or engine scheduling frequency."
